      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "PostgreSQL fixed CVE-2026-6473, integer wraparound in several server features that undersizes an allocation and writes out of bounds, in 17.10. Within major version 17, releases before 17.10 are affected. https://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-6473/, https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/17.10/. Debian's postgresql-17 17.10-0+deb13u1 upload packages PostgreSQL 17.10, and its changelog entry lists CVE-2026-6473 (https://metadata.ftp-master.debian.org/changelogs//main/p/postgresql-17/postgresql-17_17.12-0+deb13u1_changelog). The Debian tracker records the trixie fix at the later 17.11-0+deb13u1 (DSA-6438-1): https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6473. The fixed version is this owner's rebuild of Debian's 17.10-0+deb13u1, which packages PostgreSQL 17.10 and is no longer in the repository. It is the boundary, rather than the lowest build published now, because this assessment's evidence includes that build and it carries the fix; a later boundary would list it as affected. Every build published now carries the fix: the postgres server binary reports PostgreSQL 17.11 in the current rebuild of Debian's 17.11-0+deb13u1 and in the 17.11-1 build, and PostgreSQL 17.12 in the 17.12-0 build and in the rebuild of Debian's 17.12-0+deb13u1, on amd64 and arm64."
